-- R3 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md, and the one operand class
-- where the keyword CANNOT be dropped even though everything in sight
-- type-checks.
--
-- `red` names two things here: a Colour constructor, and a GIVEN carrying a
-- Colour. The two spellings of the action disagree, and both are legal:
--
--   MUST paint (EXACTLY red)   -- EXACTLY evaluates `red` as an expression,
--                                 which finds the GIVEN, i.e. whatever colour
--                                 was supplied
--   MUST paint red             -- R1 row 1: a name that is also a constructor
--                                 is the constructor pattern, i.e. the colour
--                                 red itself
--
-- The traces below supply green for the GIVEN and then paint green. The first
-- rule is discharged; the second is not. So a deprecation warning offering
-- "write `red` in place of the EXACTLY" here would silently change which
-- events discharge the obligation -- which is what the warning did until the
-- review of 2026-09-16. It now refuses to offer the drop, and says why.
--
-- The residual printed by the second trace is the other half of the same
-- hazard (§6): the printer keeps EXACTLY for a pinned pattern whose source
-- wrote it, because dropping it there would re-parse as the constructor.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer

DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF
    red
    green

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    paint HAS c IS A Colour

GIVEN red IS A Colour
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the colour supplied` MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST paint (EXACTLY red) WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH

GIVEN red IS A Colour
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the colour red` MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST paint red WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH

-- supplied green, painted green: the reference is satisfied, the constructor
-- pattern is not
#TRACE `the colour supplied` green AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Buyer DOES paint green AT 1
#TRACE `the colour red` green AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Buyer DOES paint green AT 1

-- supplied green, painted red: the other way round
#TRACE `the colour supplied` green AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Buyer DOES paint red AT 1
#TRACE `the colour red` green AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Buyer DOES paint red AT 1
